course: dictionary
lesson: 13697
title: Insect eaters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insectivorous is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Insect means a small animal with six legs, and -vorous comes from a word meaning eating. So insectivorous means eating insects as the main food.
explain: «The bat is insectivorous, so it catches moths in the night air.» The clue is that the bat hunts moths, which are insects. Ask yourself: what does the bat mostly eat? Insects, so the word fits.
explain: Compare the other -vorous words: herbivorous means eating plants, carnivorous means eating meat, and omnivorous means eating both. If you know these, you can often guess a new one.
fact: Insectivorous means eating insects as the main food.
fact: Bats, swallows, frogs, hedgehogs, anteaters and many lizards are insectivorous animals.
fact: Venus flytraps and sundews are insectivorous plants: they catch insects to get nutrients from poor soil.
fact: An insectivore is an animal that eats insects. In a food chain, insectivores are consumers.
fact: Herbivorous means eating plants, carnivorous means eating meat, and omnivorous means eating both.
exercise: «The bat is insectivorous, so it catches moths in the night air.» What does insectivorous mean? | Eating meat and plants | Flying only at night | *Eating insects as the main food | Eating plants as the main food
exercise: Which word means eating plants as the main food? | insectivorous | *herbivorous | carnivorous | omnivorous
exercise: Which of these is an insectivorous animal? | *A swallow | A lion | A cow
test: «Venus flytraps are insectivorous plants that catch insects to get nutrients from poor soil.» Why do Venus flytraps catch insects? | To keep the soil warm | *To get nutrients from poor soil | To grow taller than trees | To give insects a home
test: Which word means eating both plants and animals? | insectivorous | carnivorous | *omnivorous | herbivorous
exam: In a food chain, what is an insectivore? | A decomposer that breaks down dead things | A producer that makes its own food | *A consumer that eats insects | A plant eaten by herbivores
